rue] [17592186397954 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397954 1084 #uuid "509a42a4-798c-5fc3-9c59-d38751cdb4c6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397955 1084 #uuid "8f2d66b0-8b30-53a5-a4be-3334a7d6f7f7" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397957 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1069 "q-109865" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1071 "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ under the action of $A+B?$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1072 #uuid "3b884b20-b24f-567b-b7d3-aeaaf2084dca" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186397956 1074 "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $A+B$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $A+B:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (a+b)_{1} & (a+b)_{2} & ⋯ & (a+b)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A+B}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A+B$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B),$ the column space of $A+B.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/02/02a739d8888f2b46b81075218693e6b2cc87e3c5b81b522ab