 1081 "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398061 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398061 1084 #uuid "bfcffbe5-1391-58fa-a758-12ee97cbeaef" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398062 1081 "B={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398062 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398062 1084 #uuid "81092aae-3b21-5088-85a1-58d891002d69" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398063 1081 "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398063 1084 #uuid "76c389fc-2968-58e5-88a2-67b42fb29a93" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398064 1081 "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398064 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398064 1084 #uuid "bc6bbfd9-40b7-5c44-af28-56d554c70bec" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398065 1081 "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398065 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398065 1084 #uuid "18530549-03b9-564b-8a59-91912e430d11" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398066 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398067 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398066 1069 "q-111398" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398066 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398066 1071 "Find a basis of the null space of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398066 1072 #uuid "7095989b-ba77-5498-ade8-c79cbe233a38" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398066 1074 "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in reduced row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are basic variables corresponding to the pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd) and ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable corresponding to the non-pivot column. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}\\in R.$ This implies that\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate the $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398068 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398069 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398070 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398071 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398072 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398071 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398067 1080 #uuid "a441ee4e-1673-5fdf-a82d-7fb25a2e1c23" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398068 1081 "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\