139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398101 1074 "Given a polynomial with integer coefficients, the rational roots theorem states that any rational roots of the polynomial must take the form\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{\\text{factor of the constant term}}{\\text{factor of the leading coefficient}}.\n$$\n\nFor the given polynomial:\n\n- The constant term is $-6,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1,$ $\\pm 2,$ $\\pm 3$ and $\\pm 6.$\n\n- The leading coefficient is $8,$ and its factors are $\\pm 1,$ $\\pm 2,$ $\\pm 4$ and $\\pm 8.$\n\nFirst, we list out all the possibilities for the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm \\frac{1}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{8}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{2}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{2}{8}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{3}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{3}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{3}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{3}{8}, \\\\ \\pm \\frac{6}{1}, & \\pm \\frac{6}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{6}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{6}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the fractions to the lowest terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{8}, \\\\ \\pm 2, & \\pm 1, & \\pm \\frac{1}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\pm 3, & \\pm \\frac{3}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{3}{4}, & \\pm \\frac{3}{8}, \\\\ \\pm 6, & \\pm 3, & \\pm \\frac{3}{2}, & \\pm \\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that several potential roots are duplicates (shown above in red). Removing these duplicates, and listing those remaining in order from least to greatest in absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n\\pm \\frac{1}{8},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{4},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{8},\\,\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{4},\\,\\pm 1,\\,\\pm \\frac{3}{2},\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 3,\\,\\pm 6.\n$$\n\nThis makes a total of $20$ potential roots. (Remember that each $\\pm $ sign accounts for $2$ roots, and $2\\cdot 10=20.$)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398103 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398104 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398105 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398106 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398107 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398103 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398102 1080 #uuid "a41a2631-5f05-5cb0-8884-5d26ad87d7dc" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398103 1081 "20" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398103 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398103 1084 #uuid "357249e1-8233-550b-a2b6-bc4c45db0b8b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398104 1081 "40" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398104 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398104 1084 #uuid "700e4dc2-6ee6-59b0-9682-ea3f212774a8" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398105 1081 "36" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398105 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398105 1084 #uuid "ee2d1b9a-efc7-5d65-a374-fde07a3ab1a0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398106 1081 "32" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398106 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398106 1084 #uuid "c5e3e4ee-78d4-585c-9966-ec729d5a520d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398107 1081 "24" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398107 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398107 1084 #uuid "06976d6f-2b76-586c-9c37-4569ff276616" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398108 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398109 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398108 1069 "q-113502" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398108 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398108 1071 "$\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398108 1072 #uuid "201b1303-edfe-5a94-b70a-3687fd03d284" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398108 1074 "Let $u=2-5x.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 18(2-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 18{u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =18\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})\\int {u}^{5}\\cdot \\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\int {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{u}^{6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}+C] & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{3}{5}(2-5x)^{6}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2-5x)+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5}(2-5x)^{5}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =18(2-5x)^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398110 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398111 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398112 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398113 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398114 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398109 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 