15 1074 "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int (x-2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet $u=x-2.$ Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u,$ calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {u}^{-3}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {u}^{-2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{u}^{2}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}+C] & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{2}}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(x-2)^{-2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (x-2)^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-2)+0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{3}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398117 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398118 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398119 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398120 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398121 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398121 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398116 1080 #uuid "c13dea0f-f218-5cd2-a503-c7b2250d51fb" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398117 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2(x-2)^{4}}+C" 1319413953347