ca465f89" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398139 1081 "(0,1)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398139 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398139 1084 #uuid "e9ada809-11e9-519c-8800-9ed02ca8d533" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398140 1081 "(0,-\\frac{1}{4})" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398140 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398140 1084 #uuid "77a1d4df-21dd-55c4-aa5e-6b99c9ef011e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398141 1081 "(-1,0)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398141 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398141 1084 #uuid "2cf0c4d3-d5f0-5202-86d5-80c8f41021ba" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398142 1081 "(\\frac{1}{4},0)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398142 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398142 1084 #uuid "4cb579ad-3bd5-5860-ac4c-55d8de9d5206" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398143 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398144 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398143 1069 "q-116051" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398143 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398143 1071 "![](images/30/30b101fa9812c49237ab72c0c4aebd1666df6de80367eb2ee59b33fe0e422d87.png)\n\nIf the diagonals of a square decrease at a rate of $3\\sqrt{2}\\text{ m}\\text{/min}$, at what rate is the perimeter decreasing?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398143 1072 #uuid "3c40d4d8-93cd-5fd9-9c9b-8b9eaffb8fe0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398143 1074 "Let $p$ be the perimeter of the square, and $h$ be the length of the diagonal. The relationship between $p$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\np=2\\sqrt{2}h.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}h}(2\\sqrt{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that each diagonal of the square is decreasing at a rate of $3\\sqrt{2}\\text{ m}\\text{/min},$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=-3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information into the above expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{2})=-12\\text{ m/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the square decreases at $12\\text{ m}/\\text{min}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398145 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398146 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398147 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398148 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398149 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398148 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398144 1080 #uuid "015670c7-de29-5d58-b9b4-055602c56ffa" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398145 1081 "24\\text{ m}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398145 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398145 1084 #uuid "daf51f91-0a6d-569d-8c03-c177edaa1dc6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398146 1081 "10\\text{ m}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398146 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398146 1084 #uuid "ad1ee6ea-b061-51dc-b501-839195b28399" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398147 1081 "6\\text{ m}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398147 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398147 1084 #uuid "6d4f5765-990d-5307-bcda-feb606bb929b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398148 1081 "12\\text{ m}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398148 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398148 1084 #uuid "58cdd8af-ecc0-5a53-9201-682ba5b6106b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398149 1081 "3\\text{ m}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398149 1084 #uuid "d97728d8-7183-59a2-bbab-433924b0cf9c" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398150 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398151 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398150 1069 "q-116499" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398150 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398150 1071 "![](images/1a/1a03b31de4f99e5e3ad4a65645beeeb067afc9fdfb0ccb39ada3aff305947f9d.png)\n\nThe length of the rectangular prism shown above is increasing at a rate of $7\\text{ in/min}.$ What is the rate of change of the surface area of the rectangular prism?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398150 1072 #uuid "d6db5db2-50cf-5e89-b77b-4e40b77e862d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398150 1074 "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the rectangular prism, and let $S$ be its surface area. The variables $x$ and $S$ change with time. In particular, we are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =8\\text{ in}, \\\\ z & =12\\text{ in}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\text{ in}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe want to find the rate of change of $S$ knowing the rate of change of $x.$ So, we start with the formula for the surface area of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nS=2xz+2xy+2yz\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get\n\n$$\nS=2(12)(x)+2x(8)+2(12)(8)=40x+192.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =40(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the above expression using $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=7,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =40(7)=280{\\text{ in}}^{2}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rectangular prism's surface area is increasing at a rate of $280\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398152 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398153 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398154 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398155 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398156 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398154 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398151 1080 #uuid "928bec64-a4b8-516a-a3c0-19b5dc92551a" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398152 1081 "246\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398152 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398152 1084 #uuid "2bf733ca-e8db-54e0-88b3-d8204cd89122" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398153 1081 "138\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398153 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398153 1084 #uuid "759c10d3-8812-51e4-b644-819a5511aa3f" 13194139533472 17592