}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{hour}.\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe relation between the two time-dependent variables, $V$ and $h,$ is given by the formula for the volume of the water in the tank:\n\n$$\nV=LWh\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides with respect to $t,$ treating both $L$ and $W$ as constants, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(V) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(LWh) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =LW\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can plug in the known values and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =(8)(4)\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =32\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the water level is rising at a rate of $8\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398159 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398160 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398161 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398162 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398163 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398160 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398158 1080 #uuid "cbaa4a7f-8da9-5213-ac9e-71081f8e7d7b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398159 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}\\text{/hour}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398159 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398159 1084 #uuid "1af0f327-7957-509c-92ce-f6ccf0ddb3d1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398160 1081 "8\\,{\\text{m}}^