2 17592186045585 true] [17592186398171 1069 "q-117796" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398171 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398171 1071 "![](images/92/9278723975d70fec73e313d0e164908ddd339231cb74f75b07c2edce14680111.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398171 1072 #uuid "5ecbe368-922d-5a9f-956d-5a27886e10df" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398171 1074 "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}-(-\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}⁡(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4\\pi }{5}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,⟹\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})}=\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $\\frac{1}{2}$ unit up. Hence, $D=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{5}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{5x}{4})+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398173 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398174 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398175 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398176 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398177 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398174 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398172 1080 #uuid "b20222d5-4d8b-5ef3-b5e6