ze the information we have:\n\n- The object falls for $t=6\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n- We can find the distance the object falls in meters as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =0.6\\,\\text{km} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\text{km}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\text{km}} \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\cancel{\\text{km}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}} \\\\  & =0.6\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =600\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nSubstituting these values into the formula and solving for $u,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =ut+\\frac{1}{2}g{t}^{2} \\\\ (600) & =u(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(9.8)(6)^{2} \\\\ 600 & =6u+176.4 \\\\ 423.6 & =6u \\\\ u & =70.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the initial velocity of the object was $u=70.6\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398397 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398398 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398399 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398400 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398401 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398401 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398396 1080 #uuid "f3a5589d-c173-52b7-aa4e-ec8dcdd731a1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398397 1081 "61.2\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398397 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398397 1084 #uuid "6c5bb798-cec3-5a92-9d75-11208ba367e5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398398 1081 "80.2\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398398 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 131