{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,u+(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,2u-v,\\,3u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-2)+(2u-v)\\cdot (2)+(3u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u-2v+4u-2v+3u-2v \\\\  & =5u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\,2x-y,\\,x+z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(5u-6v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398522 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398523 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398524 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398525 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398526 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398526 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398521 1080 #uuid "d15555d0-ef8f-523d-8686-3e2c75b76cda" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398522 1081 "-2u+v" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398522 1084 #uuid "82fdd23c-cc42-585e-88f4-5b182b40e621" 13194139533472 1759218604