,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing part of the expression?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398568 1072 #uuid "e0d14173-8029-50a6-8f00-d7853c057071" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398568 1074 "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z) \\\\  & =y+2+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+y+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}({x}^{2}+y+2)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,{x}^{2}+y+2\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398570 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398571 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398572 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398573 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398574 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398574 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398569 1080 #uuid "196954bd-17a6-525e-a3ea-36557f290435" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398570 1081 "2x+y+1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398570 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186