ace $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-yz)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4xz) \\\\  & =2x-z+4x \\\\  & =6x-z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(6x-z)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,6x-z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398577 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398578 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398579 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398580 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398581 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398579 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398576 1080 #uuid "5b4c4f1b-ebdf-554c-9f5f-c8043f8e6124" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398577 1081 "2x+3z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398577 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398577 1084 #uuid "fc53f04c-d5bb-59dd-b389-8e0eefab0229" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398578 1081 "2x-z+4" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398578 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398578 1084 #uuid "af12ea26-8299-5100-8312-7691bb7b67f0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398579 1081 "6x-z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398579 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398579 1084 #uuid "958be202-ad70-5f65-942d-3cf053018cf9" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398580 1081 "6x+4z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398580 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398580 1084 #uuid "221c39d4-97a7-58e1-af0f-bd5bd145ae18" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398581 1081 "2x-y-2z" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398581 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398581 1084 #uuid "fc84079a-9c1c-54c9-bc3c-5fd874d6a1dc" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398582 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398583 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398582 1069 "q-162644" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398582 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398582 1071 "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(t+1)\\,i+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)\\,j+{e}^{-t}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398582 1072 #uuid "b2987e81-f85b-5262-9ea2-835ea44d86e0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398582 1074 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398584 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398585 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398586 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398587 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398588 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398584 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398583 1080 #uuid "4112b8f8-a1d3-5ca1-a272-50f00bc81e5d" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398584 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398584 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398584 1084 #uuid "bfa1654c-e948-5fc3-a89a-4fe52cc8fccf" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398585 1081 "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398585 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398585 1084 #uuid "8d1b7514-50b8-5ddd-9dc3-5b90007cd7cf" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398586 1081 "3\\pi n" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398586 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398586 1084 #uuid "61124a49-e750-5eed-9f63-4fab70f48c25" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398587 1081 "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398587 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398587 1084 #uuid "282a04d7-5121-553a-8c70-66602f8c83db" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398588 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398588 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398588 1084 #uuid "4a1c8270-8fd2-50fc-8447-30acc60e9312" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398589 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398590 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398589 1069 "q-163839" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398589 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398589 1071 "![](images/b9/b99ff5d9d55de34b2cb3e2176e7c4171a5583e1e010626796c3ca2f9d9ed29cb.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $z=f(x,y)$ is shown above.\nWhat is the global maximum of the function?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398589 1072 #uuid "7c94f5db-a52d-5269-9d70-48b35e30ba08" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398589 1074 "First, we recall the following definitions:\n\n- The global maximum of a function is the largest value it attains on its domain. There can only be (at most) one global maximum.\n\n- A global maximum point is a point $(x,y,z)$ where a function reaches a global maximum. There can be zero, one, or many global maximum points.\n\nFor our function, the maximum value reached by the function is $f(x,y)=10.$ Therefore, the global maximum is $10.$ The function reaches this value at both $(x,y)=(2,4)$ and $(x,y)=(-4,4).$\n\n![](images/bf/bf82159ccb39f6c07fa870abe04911847dcbb240bd1cf5e6be8a1216fa9cf327.png)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398591 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398592 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398593 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398594 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398595 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398592 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398590 1080 #uuid "ea34e434-1d65-55e5-98c8-c4dc723100a6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398591 1081 "12" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398591 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398591 1084 #uuid "43d7fcb0-ff70-592c-ad54-21abfd7d0ab1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398592 1081 "10" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398592 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398592 1084 #uuid "b69485bc-fe91-5715-a1be-f3a4cae4eec7" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398593 1081 "8" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398593 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398593 1084 #uuid "0fd4e3aa-8ad0-50a4-8f3f-5869b4c7e1f2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398594 1081 "6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398594 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398594 1084 #uuid "5b5ce768-561a-530a-b18b-d90e38f2f278" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398595 1081 "4" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398595 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398595 1084 #uuid "1d2fdced-3009-5582-9920-2ae6deb17073" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398596 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398597 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398596 1069 "q-164249" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398596 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398596 1071 "What is the radius of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z=12?$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398596 1072 #uuid "16dea1c4-5f05-52d5-8897-db965a563c2b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398596 1074 "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z & =12 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+({z}^{2}-4z+4) & =12+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}={4}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $4.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398598 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398599 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398600 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398601 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398602 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398601 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398597 1080 #uuid "894e1641-4cda-5256-a33c-65967a2846fc" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398598 1081 "3" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398598 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398598 1084 #uuid "99ff0bee-2eb2-50e8-87cd-b7fd103093fe" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398599 1081 "6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398599 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398599 1084 #uuid "72a9aeba-e4a8-5fb4-952f-d24c797294fd" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398600 1081 "2\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398600 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398600 1084 #uuid "dd6ec8be-4e28-5339-a7f2-8fd7158128e6" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398601 1081 "4" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398601 1083 #edb/ref