ional number \n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$ \n\nThe sentence\n\n$-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the sentence\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}$ is **not** a rational number, or $-2$ is negative\n\ncan be expressed symbolically as $¬P∨Q.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398639 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398640 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398641 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398642 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398643 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398642 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398638 1080 #uuid "4aa8db07-0769-5153-9ab7-dcb3cda6e4d9" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398639 1081 "¬P∧Q" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398639 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398639 1084 #uuid "ca03f4c6-f43c-599e-ae00-4805c10c1a34" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398640 1081 "¬P∨¬Q" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398640 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398640 1084 #uuid "6c488ba2-23ee-5b95-ab2f-5cc4c289bd14" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398641 1081 "¬(P∨Q)" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398641 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398641 1084 #uuid "04dfe78b-c811-5b57-8684-5e4f44c6e6fe" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398642 1081 "¬P∨Q" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398642 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398642 1084 #uuid "253f3d0c-3686-58c6-b0b3-fee8f8709936" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398643 1081 "¬P∧¬Q" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398643 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398643 1084 #uuid "6f871f5a-c1eb-5f12-8176-b04fd5f551f7" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398644 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398645 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398644 1069 "q-178256" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398644 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398644 1071 "Which root(s) of the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-25x+125$ have multiplicity $2?$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398644 1072 #uuid "d601c130-3a93-5630-8b35-93cbbfae4d1b" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398644 1074 "First, we need to factor the polynomial. For this polynomial, we can factor by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & ={x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-25x+125 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x-5)-25(x-5) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-25)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+5)(x-5)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x-5{)}^{2}(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the roots and their multiplicities, we look at the factors:\n\n- The factor $(x-5)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$\n\n- The factor $(x+5)$ has an exponent of $1$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=-5$ has multiplicity $1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398646 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398647 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398648 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398649 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398650 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398647 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398645 1080 #uuid "7a80fbe4-dbfb-530c-af35-e0f30a4a5542" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398646 1081 "x=-5,\\,5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398646 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398646 1084 #uuid "49f83912-5796-573a-b936-a61ffb603ff7" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398647 1081 "x=5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398647 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398647 1084 #uuid "b6a7c8bb-09ff-5a0f-b690-cf0f292ac7ee" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398648 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398648 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398648 1084 #uuid "d012c549-4023-5194-9620-c38392bb0ca8" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398649 1081 "x=-\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398649 1084 #uuid "1ca07054-2359-5a47-9068-5f524310351e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398650 1081 "x=-5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398650 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398650 1084 #uuid "d7f9a8cc-12c2-5db4-9c8e-f8300024f0d2" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398651 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398652 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398651 1069 "q-178288" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398651 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398651 1071 "Use the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(1+x)^{7}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(0.99)^{7}.$ Give your answer to four decimal places." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398651 1072 #uuid "1dd05574-640c-5b9b-a9a5-c23bbe5e5973" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398651 1074 "Recall that when $n$ is a positive integer, \n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{1}{2!}n(n-1){x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+x)}^{7} & =1+7x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot {x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{7} \\\\  & =1+7x+21{x}^{2}+⋯+{x}^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{7}≈1+7x+21{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=-0.01$ into the above approximation of $(1+x)^{7}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0.99)^{7} & =(1+(-0.01))^{7} \\\\  & ≈1+7(-0.01)+21(-0.01)^{2} \\\\  & =1-7(0.01)+21(0.000\\,1) \\\\  & =1-0.07+0.002\\,1 \\\\  & =0.932\\,1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto four decimal places." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398653 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398654 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398655 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398656 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398657 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398657 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398652 1080 #uuid "64422b03-65b9-5eba-85ad-d054b042f1a5" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398653 1081 "0.832\\,0" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398653 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398653 1084 #uuid "0bb84096-c5db-5ab5-b2a4-918374d6c439" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398654 1081 "1.072\\,1" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398654 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398654 1084 #uuid "f40f63d2-b3e6-582d-ab41-031f7f8b7c5f" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398655 1081 "1.067\\,9" 1319413953347