80 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398684 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398685 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398681 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398680 1080 #uuid "d5bb647b-4cce-5754-83fc-4c7a4d164719" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398681 1081 "{2,{2},4,{2,4}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398681 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398681 1084 #uuid "1f594351-7d69-5b82-ab56-b4db6aaba670" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398682 1081 "{2,4}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398682 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398682 1084 #uuid "3e5dcf18-a6b9-553b-a871-0bc3c2718b05" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398683 1081 "{{2},{2,4}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398683 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398683 1084 #uuid "de1759b9-e64e-5632-a63d-7d4aa37be03e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398684 1081 "{2,4,{2,4}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398684 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398684 1084 #uuid "da14cc2c-21a9-55db-9d59-5d5696de6caa" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398685 1081 "{2,{2},{4},{2,4}}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398685 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398685 1084 #uuid "b87b006b-5e3d-5087-a977-1843b650269c" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398687 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1069 "q-31633" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1071 "The acceleration $a$ at time $t$ of a particle $P$ moving in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\na=⟨5,3⟩,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nGiven that the particle has velocity $v=⟨-5,-3⟩$ when $t=2,$ calculate the times at which the particle is stationary." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1072 #uuid "359dea7b-c28c-5695-9f78-2decd6212dc8" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398686 1074 "The particle is stationary when its velocity is zero. So first, we need to compute the velocity of the particle.\n\nTo compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int ⟨5,3⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨\\int 5\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 3\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5t+{C}_{1},\\,3t+{C}_{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(2)=⟨-5,-3⟩.$ Substituting $t=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =⟨5(2)+{C}_{1},\\,3(2)+{C}_{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨-5,-3⟩ & =⟨10+{C}_{1},\\,6+{C}_{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso we must have ${C}_{1}=-15$ and ${C}_{2}=-9.$ Therefore, the velocity is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =⟨5t-15,\\,3t-9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the times at which the particle is stationary, we solve for the times at which the velocity is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨5t-15,\\,3t-9⟩ & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5t-15 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=3, \\\\ 3t-9 & =0\\,⇒\\,t=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution that satisfies both equations is $t=3,$ so this is the only value of $t$ when the particle is stationary." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398688 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398689 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398690 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398691 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [1759218639