592186398718 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398718 1084 #uuid "2bec3acc-bb2d-57e7-9c8e-901bc98b88ff" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398719 1068 #edb/ref 17592186398720 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398719 1069 "q-326236" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398719 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398719 1071 "Consider the system of linear differential equations given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t).\n$$\n\nGiven that the solution to the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398719 1072 #uuid "17c5a462-c29c-5b82-b891-ee8c95c1220f" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398719 1074 "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince $A$ is lower-triangular, the repeated eigenvalue is $\\lambda =-1$ (of multiplicity two).\nFor this eigenvalue, we get \n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n$v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda $ and only one linearly independent eigenvector $v$, the solution of the system of differential equations is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nTo find $w,$ we solve the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A-\\lambda I)w & =v \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-1-(-1) & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1-(-1)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1} \\\\ {w}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last equality allows us to form the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{w}_{1}+0{w}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n{w}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe variable ${w}_{2}$ is a free variable. Setting ${w}_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nw=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{-t}+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}),\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, we see that $a=0,b=\\frac{1}{3},$ and $a+b=\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398721 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398722 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398723 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398724 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1075 #edb/ref 17592186398725 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1079 #edb/ref 17592186398724 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398720 1080 #uuid "12200322-ef19-5f83-936e-a28151c6b492" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398721 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398721 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398721 1084 #uuid "c1570ae2-7522-574c-b09e-cc0720cebf4e" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186398722 1081 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 