}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399063 1072 #uuid "21067b43-552c-57fe-bdc4-8f094139d29a" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399063 1074 "Recall that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},$ therefore the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{7}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{2}{7})=106.601\\,549{…}^{∘}≈{106.602}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${106.602}^{∘}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={106.602}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the second quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={73.398}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={73.398}^{∘}.$\n\n![](images/e3/e378560486eca17f870b21743718c9f984f2bd3bf5609601f1cea674e15018e6.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{73.398}^{∘} \\\\  & ={253.398}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=106.602\\cdot 253.398≈27\\,013,\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399065 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399066 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399067 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399068 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399069 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399064 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186