 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399234 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399235 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399234 1069 "q-85966" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399234 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399234 1071 "![](images/8e/8e03226558b1dbb2e93d23947b0b05f3d8413dc35207bbe9b536e68108f40955.png)\n\nThe length of a rectangular prism is decreasing by $3\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min},$ while the $5\\,\\text{cm}$ height does not change. If the volume of the rectangular prism is increasing at a rate of $15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min},$  how fast is its width changing when its dimensions are $6\\,\\text{cm}$ in length and $2\\,\\text{cm}$ in width?" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399234 1072 #uuid "179e9be2-d5dc-5bf7-a08f-f77d3bd121bf" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399234 1074 "Let $x,y,z$ be the dimensions of the solid, and let $V$ be its volume. We are given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ y & =2\\,\\text{cm}, \\\\ z & =5\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-3\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe would like to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ when $x=6\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=2\\,\\text{cm}$ and $z=5\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nWe start with the formula for the volume of the rectangular prism:\n\n$$\nV=xyz\n$$\n\nSince $z$ is not changing and $z=5,$ we get\n\n$$\nV=5xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5xy) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =5x(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+5y(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =5(6)(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})+5(2)(-3) \\\\ 15 & =30(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})-30 \\\\ 45 & =30(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{cm}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the width of the solid is increasing at a rate of $\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}$ at the moment when $x=6\\,\\text{cm},$ $y=2\\,\\text{cm}$ and $z=5\\,\\text{cm}.$" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399236 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399237 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399238 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399239 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399240 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1077 "selection" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1079 #edb/ref 17592186399239 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399235 1080 #uuid "c119d922-a10c-5cfb-9f5d-697a1f5368d3" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399236 1081 "1\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399236 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399236 1084 #uuid "dae026cc-2f8b-57ac-b71d-10c48af3c603" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399237 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399237 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399237 1084 #uuid "2fff83ba-a026-5a48-a91c-bd58ef842ecb" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399238 1081 "2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{min}" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399238 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [17592186399238 1084 #uuid "6242ac02-1910-5a41-abad-40594fc76cee" 13194139533472 17592186045585 true] [175921863992